// Negative twin of 0272: pin `server` to a literal that no
// Login event in the trace ever uses. The expected result is zero
// permits; the literal-pin filter is what we are testing. An
// implementation that ignored the literal-equality condition, or applied it
// at the wrong position, would let the Read events permit anyway.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: "never-existed" }
};
